  "openQuestions": [
    "resolveCopayCode ($dn) applies the 2-other-disease block only when the patient has no rows for the selected disease, while prescriptionEligibility (Cdn) applies it first unconditionally. With history [01 Y 5, 02 Y 3, 04 Y 1] the copay code is G but the UI says 처방불가. Which is intended? Looks like a bug in $dn.",
    "The 20-day threshold is hard-coded in both Cdn and $dn ('>= 20' -> U / warning). Is 20 the regulatory per-disease benefit cap (and should it be a regulatory-limits reference value)?",
    "When rows for the same disease mix 'Y' and 'N', N0e marks the merged record 'Y' and uses the max days, so other-clinic history is hidden as soon as this clinic has any row. Intended?",
    "On the web build only one row (the selected disease) is fetched, so the 2-other-disease rule can never fire on web; only the desktop app (HIRA selectPatPcmdList with code '00') returns all diseases.",
    "Timing: $dn runs in a watch on the disease code using whatever history is cached at that moment; on web the history is fetched after $dn runs, so the first selection uses stale/empty history. The server should evaluate against fresh HIRA data.",
    "N0e normalizes any registration flag that is not 'Y' (including '' from the web fallback when the API omits it) to 'N', so a row with an unknown flag and days > 0 is treated as other-clinic history and blocks prescribing. Intended, or should unknown be treated as no data?",
    "Message text appends '으로' regardless of the final consonant (e.g. '안면신경마비으로'). Cosmetic, but server messages may differ.",
    "History is queried for new Date().getFullYear() (current calendar year), not the encounter year; editing a prior-year chart early in January uses this year's history.",
    "A disease code not present in M0e (anything other than 00-06) with a matching history row throws TypeError in Cdn."
